## Key Design Decisions

- **Standard AIME methodology**: `\boxed{}` extraction → pass@1 exact-match integer scoring (0–999)
- **Batch strategy**: Baseline & Continuous batched (`batch_size=8`), Dynamic_Spherical sequential (per-sequence PID state)
- **Separate datasets**: each [.jsonl](file:///f:/academic/Closed-Loop-Steering-System/src/dataset/aime2025.jsonl) runs independently via `--dataset` arg for parallel GPU execution

## Usage

```bash
# Run on AIME 2025 dataset
python run_experiment.py --dataset ./dataset/aime2025.jsonl

# Run on AIME 2026 dataset (in a separate terminal, parallel GPU)
python run_experiment.py --dataset ./dataset/aime2026.jsonl

# Run only specific modes
python run_experiment.py --dataset ./dataset/aime2025.jsonl --modes Baseline Dynamic_Spherical
```

Results are saved to `./results/aime2025/` and `./results/aime2026/` respectively.

